<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Apple-Support-Community.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="brief size-full wp-image-1076860" align="left" style="float:left;margin:0 20px 20px 0;width:160px;height:auto;" />Apple previously announced that the Apple Support Community would be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/10/apple-support-community-closing-november-20/">permanently closing on November 20</a>. The discussion forums were placed into a read-only state on November 10 and have now been removed entirely. If you visit <a href="https://discussions.apple.com/">discussions.apple.com</a>, you will be redirected to the main Apple Support page. However, the <a href="https://communities.apple.com/fr">French</a> and <a href="https://communities.apple.com/de">German</a> forums are still accepting posts for now.<div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-support-communities/">Apple Support Communities</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/21/rip-apple-support-community/">RIP, Apple Support Community</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/rip-apple-support-community.2494930/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>